WEBVTT

00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:04.950
Oh, Greco.

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:08.360
What? Hold on.

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:14.000
He... He lost?

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:16.930
The last World Tournament champion,

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:20.070
Carlos Kaiser himself...!

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:22.270
<i>﻿Who was the opponent?</i>

00:00:22.610 --> 00:00:24.510
It was Team Nemesis.

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:27.010
<i>﻿Are you saying that Gawain won?</i>

00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:28.680
No, not him.

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:30.610
What!?

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:34.280
The winner was a girl around my age?

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:40.390
It serves that Kaiser right.

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:42.360
Don't you agree, brother?

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:49.870
Kaiser lost...

00:00:49.870 --> 00:00:53.970
Does that mean my biggest
obstacle is now eliminated?

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:01.840
That can't be.

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:04.750
Even with our information
gathering capabilities,

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:07.780
we don't know anything
about Nemesis's top fighter.

00:01:09.890 --> 00:01:13.960
Who on earth is she?

00:02:55.890 --> 00:02:56.590
Reiji!

00:02:57.600 --> 00:02:59.000
Are you alright, Reiji!?

00:02:59.230 --> 00:03:00.360
Hold on!

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:02.930
- Unbelievable...
- ﻿What?

00:03:05.470 --> 00:03:10.410
Sei has built an unbelievable Gunpla!

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:20.550
Hello, everyone!

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:24.590
Chosen as the image character for the
Gunpla Championship World Tournament,

00:03:24.590 --> 00:03:26.460
I'm Kirara, the Gunpla idol!

00:03:26.830 --> 00:03:27.890
Kiraran!

00:03:28.130 --> 00:03:31.060
Hey Reiji, Miss Mihoshi's on TV.

00:03:31.660 --> 00:03:33.730
I'm not surprised.

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:38.900
She's a woman who does
what she says she'll do.

00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:42.770
Right now I'm in Shizuoka City,
in Shizuoka Prefecture.

00:03:42.770 --> 00:03:48.580
I'm at the arena where tomorrow,
the World Tournament will begin.

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:51.320
This is the 7th World Tournament.

00:03:51.550 --> 00:03:55.720
More than 80 Gunpla fighters from
68 countries will gather here,

00:03:55.720 --> 00:04:01.660
to fight exciting battles and
strive for the championship.

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:05.930
Let me briefly explain
the tournament rules.

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:10.970
The contestants will earn points
through several kinds of battle,

00:04:10.970 --> 00:04:15.340
such as individual, team and
endurance matches.

00:04:15.340 --> 00:04:20.140
The 16 fighters with the most points
will advance to the final tournament,

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:22.750
and attempt to become champion.

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:26.680
Sei and Reiji, Mr. Ral's here.

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:31.960
Thank you for picking us up
and giving us a ride, Mr. Ral.

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:33.620
No problem at all.

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:36.860
I was going to go see it
from the opening ceremony anyway.

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:42.000
Mr. Ral, please look after them well.

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:45.170
Leave it to me, Mrs. Rinko.

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:49.810
You two, do your best,
so you won't regret anything.

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:51.810
- Yeah.
- Count on me!

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:54.780
Iori! Reiji!

00:04:54.780 --> 00:04:56.480
Kousaka.

00:04:57.280 --> 00:04:58.220
Iori.

00:04:58.850 --> 00:04:59.820
Here.

00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:02.250
Wow, cool!

00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:04.620
- What's that?
- ﻿It's a charm.

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:06.520
There's one for you, too.

00:05:06.930 --> 00:05:09.760
I assume Sei's was the main one,

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:11.230
but thanks.

00:05:12.860 --> 00:05:14.570
I'll catch up and go cheer for you.

00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:19.470
Thanks, Kousaka!

00:05:25.540 --> 00:05:26.580
This is it.

00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:30.080
Reiji's and my...

00:05:30.250 --> 00:05:32.050
Our World Tournament!

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:40.260
This is the players' village
where you'll stay.

00:05:40.630 --> 00:05:43.160
But by the 10th day of the tournament,

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:46.100
70% of the fighters
will be gone from here.

00:05:50.570 --> 00:05:52.640
May you two survive!

00:05:58.610 --> 00:06:00.840
What's with these clothes, Sei?

00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:02.610
I told you.

00:06:02.610 --> 00:06:05.620
PPSE, the organizer of
the World Tournament,

00:06:05.620 --> 00:06:10.250
is having a reception party for
the players and tournament staff.

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:12.920
We've all been asked to dress up.

00:06:12.920 --> 00:06:14.390
A party?

00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:17.230
I don't like formal stuff.

00:06:17.530 --> 00:06:19.600
Just change already.

00:06:22.670 --> 00:06:25.540
If I do say so myself...

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:28.070
This really doesn't suit me.

00:06:28.940 --> 00:06:30.970
Reiji, are you—

00:06:36.770 --> 00:06:38.250
Re...

00:06:39.880 --> 00:06:42.750
Reiji!

00:06:45.820 --> 00:06:47.460
Sorry, Sei.

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:50.230
Your mom gave me some funds.

00:06:50.230 --> 00:06:52.900
I'm off to go wherever I like.

00:06:59.270 --> 00:07:02.870
Welcome, Mr. Sei Iori.
Please go inside.

00:07:02.870 --> 00:07:05.310
Y-Yes. Thank you very much.

00:07:10.350 --> 00:07:12.650
W-Wow.

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:19.660
Everybody here came from all over
the world to play Gunpla Battle.

00:07:21.230 --> 00:07:22.590
Mr. Sei.

00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:24.530
Long time no see.

00:07:24.530 --> 00:07:26.500
Last time we met was at the beach.

00:07:26.730 --> 00:07:27.800
Mao!

00:07:28.330 --> 00:07:31.340
I can see it in your eyes.

00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:35.440
You've completed your Gunpla
for the World Tournament, huh?

00:07:35.440 --> 00:07:36.970
Just wait and see.

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:42.350
That's Luang Dallara.

00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:46.280
He's the Thai champion,
and a World Tournament veteran.

00:07:46.580 --> 00:07:49.490
Yeah, I've seen him in magazines.

00:07:49.490 --> 00:07:51.690
Mr. Sei, look over there!

00:07:52.520 --> 00:07:54.190
It's Ricardo Fellini.

00:07:54.390 --> 00:07:56.190
The Italian Dandy.

00:07:56.190 --> 00:07:58.100
Wow, he's so good-looking.

00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:01.330
Hey, Sei Iori!

00:08:02.600 --> 00:08:04.070
He knows my name!?

00:08:04.070 --> 00:08:06.100
It's amazing, Mr. Sei!

00:08:06.100 --> 00:08:09.510
Ricardo Fellini knows who you are!

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:12.680
Reiji isn't with you?

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:16.550
Mr. Fellini, you know Reiji?

00:08:16.820 --> 00:08:18.680
I don't just know him,

00:08:18.680 --> 00:08:21.050
he put me through the wringer.

00:08:21.990 --> 00:08:25.060
Were you the one who
gave Reiji his tough training?

00:08:25.690 --> 00:08:28.360
- That was me.
- I didn't know!

00:08:28.360 --> 00:08:29.560
Thank you so much.

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:34.700
I mean,
he must bother you a lot.

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:35.730
Doesn't he?

00:08:36.130 --> 00:08:39.740
Um... Not that much...

00:08:39.740 --> 00:08:41.410
I'm so sorry.

00:08:41.840 --> 00:08:44.840
H-Hi, I'm Mao Yasaka!

00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:47.580
I know you.

00:08:47.580 --> 00:08:51.380
You're a student of Master Chinan
of the Gunpla Shingyo School, right?

00:08:51.380 --> 00:08:53.280
Do you know my master?

00:08:53.620 --> 00:08:55.250
Yeah, a little bit.

00:08:56.820 --> 00:08:58.760
Long time no see, Sei.

00:09:02.930 --> 00:09:06.260
Congratulations for making it
to the World Tournament.

00:09:08.030 --> 00:09:09.370
Who's she?

00:09:09.370 --> 00:09:12.170
Sh-She's Kirara, the Gunpla idol.

00:09:12.170 --> 00:09:13.940
What? Oh yeah!

00:09:14.310 --> 00:09:17.470
You seem to be busy, Miss Mihoshi.

00:09:17.480 --> 00:09:20.040
Yeah, I saw you on TV!

00:09:21.780 --> 00:09:25.880
Yes, I must use this opportunity
to become a top idol...

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:29.320
What's your name, miss?

00:09:29.620 --> 00:09:30.620
Huh?

00:09:31.290 --> 00:09:33.490
Well... It's Kirara, but...

00:09:35.790 --> 00:09:37.390
What a charming name.

00:09:41.870 --> 00:09:46.370
Just like in Gunpla Battle,
he's as fast as lightning.

00:09:50.510 --> 00:09:53.740
Excuse me, sir.
Aila isn't in her room.

00:09:55.310 --> 00:09:58.250
Yes, I'll go search for her right now.

00:10:09.930 --> 00:10:11.630
Please come again.

00:10:11.830 --> 00:10:14.330
That was so yummy!

00:10:14.930 --> 00:10:16.930
Grilled eel on rice is so good.

00:10:17.540 --> 00:10:22.470
The next tasty dish that
old man Ral told me about is...

00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:30.550
Can I have some of those
baked sweet-sticks?

00:10:30.550 --> 00:10:33.580
I'm sorry. We just sold out.

00:10:35.550 --> 00:10:36.690
Oh, man...

00:10:40.530 --> 00:10:42.890
One turtle sweet bun, please!

00:10:42.890 --> 00:10:44.430
They're sold out today.

00:10:45.400 --> 00:10:46.660
Again!?

00:10:53.740 --> 00:10:55.570
- One meat bun!
- ﻿Meat bun, please!

00:11:00.240 --> 00:11:02.010
Miss Kirara!

00:11:02.880 --> 00:11:06.780
Did you see that 08th MS Team
bonus video?

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:10.320
That smooth animation must
have used so many inbetweens!

00:11:10.320 --> 00:11:12.890
- Don't you think? Yes?
- What? Um...

00:11:12.890 --> 00:11:14.360
Yeah, I guess.

00:11:14.360 --> 00:11:16.130
You think?

00:11:18.130 --> 00:11:20.260
Yes, it's amazing!

00:11:20.260 --> 00:11:22.970
- I'm disillusioned.
- ﻿Yeah.

00:11:27.650 --> 00:11:29.150
Baked sweet-sticks and sweet buns!?

00:11:29.750 --> 00:11:33.620
So you're the one who's been
buying all the food around here.

00:11:33.620 --> 00:11:36.020
Don't say it like that.

00:11:36.020 --> 00:11:38.060
Um... Excuse me.

00:11:38.590 --> 00:11:41.190
There are a lot of people
here for the tournament,

00:11:41.190 --> 00:11:43.260
so there's only one left.

00:11:43.530 --> 00:11:45.430
- Then give it to me!
- Then give it to me!

00:11:47.330 --> 00:11:48.600
Give it up!

00:11:49.630 --> 00:11:51.270
No, you give up.

00:11:51.870 --> 00:11:55.040
You've already had a lot!

00:11:55.040 --> 00:11:57.610
Don't you know it's "ladies first"?

00:11:57.610 --> 00:11:59.580
Men should respect the ladies.

00:12:00.410 --> 00:12:03.450
A lady? I don't see any here.

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:04.750
Do you see any?

00:12:05.080 --> 00:12:07.450
Are you asking for a fight?

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:10.590
I'm not asking, I'm insisting!

00:12:10.920 --> 00:12:12.520
Can't you keep your mouth shut?

00:12:12.860 --> 00:12:14.460
Why, you—!

00:12:19.130 --> 00:12:20.300
Wh-What!?

00:12:22.200 --> 00:12:23.700
Keep the change!

00:12:23.700 --> 00:12:24.630
Come again.

00:12:27.170 --> 00:12:29.010
You...!

00:12:49.990 --> 00:12:51.660
Who is that girl?

00:13:01.740 --> 00:13:04.040
You'll never keep up with me.

00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:14.020
You think you can get away from me?

00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:15.250
How?

00:13:15.550 --> 00:13:18.050
Just give me this...

00:13:18.120 --> 00:13:19.390
Keep off me!

00:13:19.390 --> 00:13:22.030
- That's mine!
- ﻿No, it's mine!

00:13:22.630 --> 00:13:26.160
You've been eating the whole time!

00:13:26.360 --> 00:13:29.130
That's none of your business!

00:13:55.060 --> 00:13:58.400
What did you do, you idiot!?

00:13:58.660 --> 00:14:00.360
That's my line!

00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:03.370
- Pay for it!
- ﻿Why should I...?

00:14:14.910 --> 00:14:15.910
Huh?

00:14:16.780 --> 00:14:18.450
Hey, wait.

00:14:21.390 --> 00:14:24.390
What on earth is up with her?

00:14:27.120 --> 00:14:28.990
Who was that boy?

00:14:29.990 --> 00:14:32.030
I don't know.

00:14:32.030 --> 00:14:35.330
Don't act on your own
during the Tournament.

00:14:35.330 --> 00:14:38.170
Don't forget that
a lot of money is invested in you.

00:14:40.200 --> 00:14:42.210
I understand.

00:14:43.440 --> 00:14:44.880
Where were you?

00:14:44.980 --> 00:14:47.440
I went out to grab a meal.

00:14:48.650 --> 00:14:51.280
Um... Care for some oden stew?

00:14:52.980 --> 00:14:54.720
I won't be fooled by that!

00:14:55.050 --> 00:14:58.260
Are you aware that tomorrow's
the first day of the tournament!?

00:15:02.230 --> 00:15:05.160
Ladies and gentlemen,
thank you for waiting.

00:15:06.060 --> 00:15:10.830
We will now begin the 7th Gunpla Battle
Championship World Tournament.

00:15:15.210 --> 00:15:18.240
The first period is a
four-player knockout match.

00:15:18.940 --> 00:15:21.980
The winners will get 4 points.

00:15:22.510 --> 00:15:25.820
Where are Mr. Sei and Mr. Reiji...?

00:15:28.290 --> 00:15:29.490
I drank too much.

00:15:30.960 --> 00:15:32.460
So disillusioned.

00:16:09.030 --> 00:16:13.060
The winner of match one is
Rainer Cziommer, representing Germany.

00:16:13.060 --> 00:16:14.930
He's earned 4 points.

00:16:27.110 --> 00:16:29.410
The winner of match three is,

00:16:29.410 --> 00:16:31.650
Luang Dallara, representing Thailand.

00:16:40.490 --> 00:16:42.390
The winner of match six is,

00:16:42.390 --> 00:16:45.130
Ricardo Fellini, representing Italy.

00:16:48.630 --> 00:16:51.970
We will now begin match seven.

00:16:52.500 --> 00:16:54.370
Finally it's her turn.

00:16:57.380 --> 00:17:00.210
The fighter who defeated Carlos Kaiser.

00:17:00.540 --> 00:17:03.180
Let's see how good she is, brother.

00:17:05.880 --> 00:17:07.650
We should fight together for now.

00:17:07.650 --> 00:17:09.790
Yeah, let's get that one first!

00:17:09.790 --> 00:17:13.220
Show us how strong you are.
You, who defeated Kaiser!

00:17:24.240 --> 00:17:25.900
What happened?

00:17:25.900 --> 00:17:27.200
Funnels?

00:17:28.170 --> 00:17:30.170
I didn't see anything.

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:33.010
That weapon is...

00:17:34.080 --> 00:17:36.510
The winner of match seven is,

00:17:36.510 --> 00:17:39.520
Aila Jyrkiainen, representing Finland.

00:17:41.220 --> 00:17:43.350
That's the power of Aila Jyrkiainen,

00:17:44.560 --> 00:17:47.260
the secret asset of Team Nemesis.

00:17:48.230 --> 00:17:51.960
Up next, representing Japan,
will be Sei Iori and Reiji...

00:17:51.960 --> 00:17:54.730
the winners of the 3rd Block qualifiers.

00:17:54.730 --> 00:17:57.930
Mrs. Rinko,
it's Iori's and Reiji's turn.

00:17:57.940 --> 00:17:58.870
Okay.

00:17:59.470 --> 00:18:02.870
Finally, they show up!

00:18:02.870 --> 00:18:05.710
They're very late. They only have
10 seconds till the match.

00:18:06.310 --> 00:18:08.450
Whoa, this is embarrassing!

00:18:08.450 --> 00:18:10.380
It must be Reiji's fault.

00:18:10.380 --> 00:18:11.610
Yeah.

00:18:12.250 --> 00:18:14.580
See, I told you yesterday!

00:18:14.590 --> 00:18:17.050
Just set the Gunpla! Hurry!

00:18:19.060 --> 00:18:21.620
That's Sei Iori's Gunpla.

00:18:21.630 --> 00:18:23.430
I can tell!

00:18:23.690 --> 00:18:26.460
Though it looks the same,
it's completely different.

00:18:28.300 --> 00:18:30.770
Sei. Reiji.

00:18:30.770 --> 00:18:32.740
Let the world know...

00:18:33.770 --> 00:18:37.170
Show them your
imagination and passion!

00:18:38.440 --> 00:18:39.710
Reiji, let's go!

00:18:40.850 --> 00:18:41.610
Okay!

00:18:42.210 --> 00:18:43.810
<i>﻿Battle start.</i>

00:18:46.020 --> 00:18:48.520
- Star Build Strike!
- ﻿Here we go!

00:18:57.500 --> 00:18:59.230
Take this!

00:19:05.200 --> 00:19:06.040
Gotcha!

00:19:10.540 --> 00:19:11.370
What!?

00:19:12.010 --> 00:19:13.380
It erased the beam?

00:19:13.840 --> 00:19:16.250
You're something, but how's this!?

00:19:26.160 --> 00:19:27.860
I knew it was new equipment!

00:19:29.060 --> 00:19:30.230
They sure amaze us.

00:19:40.270 --> 00:19:40.470
- They did it!
- ﻿Wow.

00:19:40.470 --> 00:19:43.840
Star Build Strike has shot down Zaku F2000!

00:19:44.610 --> 00:19:46.540
I didn't know such a Gunpla existed.

00:19:46.540 --> 00:19:48.380
Who's the fighter?

00:19:52.180 --> 00:19:53.220
They're...

00:19:55.090 --> 00:19:56.190
From back then!

00:19:58.690 --> 00:20:00.620
Go, funnels!

00:20:11.200 --> 00:20:14.000
Darn, this is never-ending.
Sei, how's the charging?

00:20:14.640 --> 00:20:17.240
Ready to go at full power!

00:20:17.240 --> 00:20:18.010
Okay!

00:20:31.890 --> 00:20:34.520
- ﻿﻿This is our...!
- Gunpla!

00:20:57.680 --> 00:21:00.920
What performance...!

00:21:12.530 --> 00:21:13.760
These moves...

00:21:15.570 --> 00:21:17.330
Just like that time...

00:21:25.980 --> 00:21:26.910
Powerful.

00:21:29.050 --> 00:21:31.850
The winners of match thirteen are,

00:21:31.850 --> 00:21:37.150
Sei Iori and Reiji,
representing Japan's 3rd Block.

00:23:14.070 --> 00:23:17.240
Mr. Sei, congratulations!
That was really amazing.

00:23:17.640 --> 00:23:19.210
Thank you.

00:23:19.210 --> 00:23:23.420
In the last match, PPSE's works team
is finally coming out.

00:23:24.890 --> 00:23:26.720
What's PPSE?

00:23:26.720 --> 00:23:29.120
The company that makes
the Gunpla Battle system.

00:23:29.520 --> 00:23:33.490
Meaning, this team knows
all about the Plavsky particle.

00:23:33.490 --> 00:23:36.630
And the one who controls
their Gunpla is,

00:23:36.630 --> 00:23:38.530
the Meijin.

00:23:39.570 --> 00:23:41.430
Meijin Kawaguchi!

00:23:41.570 --> 00:23:44.000
- Meijin...
- ﻿Kawaguchi...?

00:23:46.340 --> 00:23:47.270
But that's...!

00:23:48.590 --> 00:23:49.210
Yu...

00:23:50.380 --> 00:23:52.310
Yuuki!?

00:23:56.200 --> 00:23:58.960
In the second period,
all players will fight at once!

00:23:58.970 --> 00:24:00.670
Next episode, "Battle Royale".

00:24:00.670 --> 00:24:03.000
We'll definitely survive, Sei!

00:24:03.000 --> 00:24:04.900
Mission accepted.
